---
import { siteConfig } from '../../config/site';
---
<section id="services" class="section services" aria-labelledby="services-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="services-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Working together</p>
        <h2 id="services-title">A little clarity<br /><em>before we begin.</em></h2>
        <p class="services-intro">Individual therapy for adults, exclusively by telehealth. Available to Washington residents only.</p>
        <p class="availability"><span aria-hidden="true"></span> Currently accepting new clients</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rates">
        <h3 class="eyebrow">Rates</h3>
        <div class="rate-row"><div><h4>Individual therapy</h4><p>53-minute session · Telehealth</p></div><span class="price">$150</span></div>
        <p>I am a private-pay therapist. Payment is due at the time of service.</p>
        <div class="consultation-row"><h4>Let&rsquo;s first see how we connect.</h4><p>A free 15-minute phone or video conversation. You can share what you&rsquo;re looking for, ask questions, and get a sense of me. We both get to consider whether it feels like a good fit.</p><p>If we decide to work together, the next step is an intake session.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href={siteConfig.contactUrl}>Request a consultation <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div id="good-faith-estimate" class="gfe">
      <h3>Good Faith Estimate</h3>
      <p>Under the federal No Surprises Act, you have the right to receive a Good Faith Estimate of the expected cost of services before your first session, and at any time upon request. I provide one to every client at scheduling. If you receive a bill at least $400 more than your Good Faith Estimate, you have the right to dispute it. Save a copy of your estimate. Learn more at{' '}
          <a href="https://www.cms.gov/nosurprises" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color:#2D5A3D;text-decoration:underline;">
            cms.gov/nosurprises
          </a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
